{"id": "EUVD-2026-59228", "enisaUuid": "4fdf42c7-c84f-3f70-835c-44769c5f203c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/liquidio: drop cached VF pci_dev LUT\n\nThe PF SR-IOV enable path caches VF pci_dev pointers in\ndpiring_to_vfpcidev_lut[] by iterating with pci_get_device(). Those\nentries do not own a reference, because the iterator drops the previous\ndevice reference on each step. The cached pointer is then dereferenced\nlater when handling OCTEON_VF_FLR_REQUEST.\n\nReplace the cached VF mapping with runtime lookup on the mailbox DPI\nring: derive the VF index from q_no, resolve the VF via exported PCI\nIOV helpers, validate it with the PF pointer and VF ID, then issue\npcie_flr() and drop the reference with pci_dev_put(). Remove the\nunused VF lookup table initialization and cleanup.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:55:39", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:44:36", "baseScore": 9.3, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e3b20de8d7c06c8f1a0ded1e52be9d282609c3da", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1cf5c6a80adc31456f3e93b2922a2446fd63e2c4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/08ff33dce6f91510bb296a753a232db0ca3fd3d8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/81acef3a247fd523513a2e9f71de1c167bc0f882", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5c0e3ba4f500fd4314ceb42f07f16bc445156431"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-72329", "GHSA-5c72-mrqj-9c57"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0ccbbe69-55c2-35f6-ab3d-17281787ffc5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ca6139ffc67ee6ef0459f81e37894ed411083855 <81acef3a247fd523513a2e9f71de1c167bc0f882"}, {"id": "17a5b878-2171-38e9-bff5-1038862a0e47", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "4761e6dc-f9fb-3943-b2ea-b5fa25ad2256", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ca6139ffc67ee6ef0459f81e37894ed411083855 <5c0e3ba4f500fd4314ceb42f07f16bc445156431"}, {"id": "62c237af-b28a-3cdf-a515-ac05a944ca44", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ca6139ffc67ee6ef0459f81e37894ed411083855 <e3b20de8d7c06c8f1a0ded1e52be9d282609c3da"}, {"id": "6b755c22-de3c-3b84-ab42-76e89c5dd521", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ca6139ffc67ee6ef0459f81e37894ed411083855 <1cf5c6a80adc31456f3e93b2922a2446fd63e2c4"}, {"id": "6cc20a65-6971-34fc-89af-3fd684950e4a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "706375ed-67f8-3484-b60d-ddf3b7b44e2b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "73293ff4-7747-3f5c-ade6-c41f16103869", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "8474536f-38a5-3ce0-980f-e1bc254b99a8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.10"}, {"id": "9d44f691-aa03-38bd-abeb-9f984728243a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ca6139ffc67ee6ef0459f81e37894ed411083855 <08ff33dce6f91510bb296a753a232db0ca3fd3d8"}, {"id": "cb6a9be6-b739-37ab-81ef-88cd89a1a757", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "ee7eb359-b8b9-3070-bfaa-c891ba1045a2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "93589d78-be36-37d2-ac9c-ba276eaa61ec", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}